{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Environment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Endangered Species"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe environmental change in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Across the world, species <span class=\"strong\">are disappearing</span> at an astonishing rate.</span></p><p>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Making laws to protect these endangered animals <span class=\"strong\">has been</span> the focus of many eco-groups. </span></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">am</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">are</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span> +  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">being </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">These products are being sold in markets around the world. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span> + <span class=\\\"italic\\\">been </span>+ past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">In many countries, endangered animals have been hunted for their valuable pelts, feathers, or meat. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Immediate action has been taken to protect the last population of many endangered species. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many countries have made laws to prohibit the hunting or killing of endangered animals. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "An increasing number of different genuses of birds, fish, and land animals are being declared extinct every year."}, {"type": "example", "content": "These products are being sold in markets around the world. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "So many of the animals have been killed that they are not able to reproduce quickly enough to continue the species."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below to compare the structure of each kind of conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Zero \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">heat</span> ice, it <span class=\\\"strong\\\">melts</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Present, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lose</span> more species, what <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be</span> the environmental cost?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Simple Past, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would</span> + Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If <span class=\\\"strong\\\">we were</span> to pollute and hunt less, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would we see</span> an immediate turn around?   </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If humans <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had been</span> more aware of wildlife preservation in the past, so many species <span class=\\\"strong\\\">wouldn't have become</span> endangered.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "astonishing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " so surprising that it is difficult to believe, alarming"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Species are disappearing at an astonishing rate."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about the species extinction."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "genus "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group into which scientists divide animals or plants"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An increasing number of different genuses of birds, fish, and land animals are being extinct every year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to declare"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to state officially and publicly that a particular situation exists or that something is true"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Scientists have had to declare the extinction of a number of species."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "remaining "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "left when others have gone, been used, or been dealt with"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Eco-groups work to keep the last remaining animals of a species alive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reproduce"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to produce new, young living beings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So many of the animals have been killed that they are not able to reproduce quickly enough."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pelt "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the skin of a dead animal, especially with the fur or hair still on it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Endangered animals have been hunted for their valuable pelts, feathers, or meat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deforestation "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the cutting or burning down of all the trees in an area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are also laws against deforestation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sympathetic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "willing to give approval and support to an aim or plan"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Not everyone is sympathetic to the cause."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or visit the library to find out which species are endangered in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a report about the kind of animal, why it has become endangered and what can be done about it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your reports with a classmate/partner. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the issue of endangered species in your country."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify endangered species in my country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about environmental issues in my country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the issue of endangered species with a partner."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about things that are happening and things that have happened. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about cause and effect, and hypothetical situations."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What endangered species are there in your country? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Why is it important to save them?"}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe environmental problems."}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"